\draw[black,dashed] (0,0)--(6,0)--(6,4);
\path (0,0) node[below left] {$(0,0)$};
\path (6,4) node[above left] {$(6,4)$};
\path (3,-0.45) node {run $=6$};
\path (6.15,2) node[right] {rise $=4$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.question_text:
The graph shows the fuel $F$ in litres used over a distance $d$ in kilometres. Use the marked points P and Q to find the gradient, write the equation relating $F$ and $d$, and interpret the gradient.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=9mm,y=9mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{mathblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[gridgrey,very thin,xstep=9mm,ystep=9mm] (0,0) grid (6,6);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(6.5,0) node[right] {$d$ (km)};
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,6.5) node[above] {$F$ (L)};
\foreach \x/\v in {1/40,2/80,3/120,4/160,5/200,6/240} {\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.08);\path (\x,-0.12) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\foreach \y/\v in {1/2,2/4,3/6,4/8,5/10,6/12} {\draw[black] (0,\y)--(-0.08,\y);\path (-0.12,\y) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\path (0,0) node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$0$};
\draw[mathblue,thick] (0,0)--(6,6);
\fill[black] (2,2) circle (1.8pt);
\fill[black] (5,5) circle (1.8pt);
\path (2,2) node[above left] {P};
\path (5,5) node[above left] {Q};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Read P as $(80,4)$ and Q as $(200,10)$.

$\begin{aligned} k&=\frac{\text{rise}}{\text{run}}\\&=\frac{10-4}{200-80}\\&=\frac{6}{120}\\&=0.05\end{aligned}$

The line passes through the origin, so $F=0.05d$.

The gradient represents fuel use of $0.05$ litres per kilometre.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=9mm,y=9mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{mathblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[gridgrey,very thin,xstep=9mm,ystep=9mm] (0,0) grid (6,6);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(6.5,0) node[right] {$d$ (km)};
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,6.5) node[above] {$F$ (L)};
\draw[mathblue,thick] (0,0)--(6,6);
\fill[black] (2,2) circle (1.8pt);
\fill[black] (5,5) circle (1.8pt);
\draw[black,dashed] (2,2)--(5,2)--(5,5);
\path (2,2) node[above left] {P $(80,4)$};
\path (5,5) node[above left] {Q $(200,10)$};
\path (3.5,1.55) node {run $=120$ km};
\path (5.15,3.5) node[right] {rise $=6$ L};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.question_text:
A plant's growth is modelled by $h=6t$, where $h$ is its increase in height in millimetres and $t$ is time in days. Complete the table for $t=0,1,2,3,4$, then draw the graph for $0\leq t\leq4$.

| $t$ (days) | 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| $h$ (mm) | | | | | |

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=12mm,y=12mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[gridgrey,very thin,xstep=12mm,ystep=12mm] (0,0) grid (4,4);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(4.5,0) node[right] {$t$ (days)};
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,4.5) node[above] {$h$ (mm)};
\foreach \x in {1,...,4} {\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.08);\path (\x,-0.12) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\v in {1/6,2/12,3/18,4/24} {\draw[black] (0,\y)--(-0.08,\y);\path (-0.12,\y) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\path (0,0) node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$0$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Substitute each time into $h=6t$. For $t=3$:

$\begin{aligned} h&=6(3)\\&=18\end{aligned}$

| $t$ (days) | 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| $h$ (mm) | 0 | 6 | 12 | 18 | 24 |

Plot $(0,0)$, $(1,6)$, $(2,12)$, $(3,18)$ and $(4,24)$, then join them with a straight line. It passes through the origin and has gradient $6$, representing growth of $6$ mm per day.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=12mm,y=12mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{mathblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
